***
***	<comment from="gemini-2.5-flash">
***	The original code uses two conditional rules (`crl`) which are mutually exclusive. This can be simplified and made more efficient by using a single unconditional rule (`rl`) with an `if_then_else_fi` operator in the right-hand side. This reduces the number of rules the Maude engine needs to consider for matching and avoids evaluating potentially multiple rule conditions.
***	</comment>
***

mod COLLATZ is	protecting NAT .
	var N : Nat .
	rl N => if N rem 2 = 0 then N quo 2 else 3 * N + 1 fi .
endm